WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.810
In 2018, the USA put a tariff of 25

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.150
per cent on imported steel.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.720
Within months, the EU hit back,

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.640
with duties on American whiskey,

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.910
motorcycles and jeans.

6
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.400
Yet economists have long
argued that free trade raises

7
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.570
total output and consumption.

8
00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.420
So if trade makes a
country richer overall,

9
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.970
why do so many governments
still choose to restrict it?

10
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:28.200
In this mission, you'll weigh
the arguments for protection,

11
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.330
from brand new industries
to national security.

12
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.010
Then you'll test each one
against the case for free trade,

13
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.730
from retaliation to higher prices.

14
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out
why protection survives.
